  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n\n## Context\nReview of pull request #449 found that `backend/packages/data/src/mail/gmailRestClient.ts` (line 95) accepts both `drive.google.com` and `docs.google.com` hostnames, but `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/gmailRestClient.unit.test.ts` only ever exercises `drive.google.com` URLs (lines 38, 60, 78, 97-98); no `docs.google.com` case exists anywhere in the file, leaving that accepted hostname's handling untested.\n\n## Task\n- Add a test case in `gmailRestClient.unit.test.ts` that exercises a `docs.google.com` URL through the same code path already covered for `drive.google.com`, asserting the same accepted behavior.\n\n## Touches\n- backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/gmailRestClient.unit.test.ts\n\n## Scope\n### In scope\n- One additional test case covering the `docs.google.com` hostname.\n\n### Out of scope\n- Any change to `gmailRestClient.ts`'s hostname-acceptance logic itself.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- A test in `gmailRestClient.unit.test.ts` exercises a `docs.google.com` URL and asserts it is accepted the same way a `drive.google.com` URL is.\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=449 key=256add7ea5 -->",
